# Git Workflow

## Commit Message Format

```
<type>: <description>

<optional body>
```

Types: feat, fix, refactor, docs, test, chore, perf, ci

Do not add AI attribution or `Co-Authored-By` lines.

## Pull Request Workflow

When creating PRs:

1. Analyze full commit history (not just latest commit)
2. Use `git diff [base-branch]...HEAD` to see all changes
3. Draft PR summary that is compact, concise, clear to the point whilst capturing the comprehensive changes.
4. Include test plan with TODOs that are one liners and easy to follow steps.
5. Push with `-u` flag if new branch

> For the full implementation and risk-based QA process before git operations,
> see [development-workflow.mdc](./development-workflow.mdc).
>
> Production releases use frozen `release-X.Y.Z` branches - see [release.mdc](./release.mdc).
> Delete merged feature branches; never delete `release-*` branches.
